# Server Config Rules

## server.cfg gotchas (learned the hard way)

- **No semicolons in comments.** FXServer parses `;` as a command separator,
  producing "No such command" errors. Use dashes instead.

```
# BAD:  ensure chat ; default resource
# GOOD: ensure chat - default resource
```

- **Enhanced accepts a single endpoint** per `endpoint_add_tcp`/`_udp`.
- `sv_master1 ""` keeps the server off the public list (private mode).
  Removing it is a Phase 3 launch action, not a casual edit.
- `ensure fivem-map-hipster` must stay before `basic-gamemode`: maps started
  dynamically by mapmanager fail cache generation on Enhanced early access.
- `exec server.cfg.local` loads local secrets - keep it after the
  placeholder keys so local values win.

## Keep template and runtime in sync

`ops/homelab/server.cfg.template` is the source of truth. When editing it,
apply the same change to the live profile at
`~/gta916/txData-enhanced/default/server.cfg` (wire-profile.sh only installs
the template when no config exists; it never overwrites).

## Scripts

- `bootstrap-enhanced.sh` / `start-server-enhanced.sh` / `wire-profile.sh
  ~/gta916 default txData-enhanced` is the Enhanced flow; legacy flow uses
  the non-suffixed scripts with default args.
- Never pre-create a txAdmin profile folder - txAdmin creates it on first
  boot (error E5110 otherwise).
- txAdmin data path is set via `TXHOST_DATA_PATH` env var, not ConVars.
